---
/** Harness loop — tsforge's edit → gate → repair cycle, not a blueprint poster. */
---

<div class="tf-loop-diagram" aria-label="How tsforge works">
  <ol class="tf-loop-diagram__steps">
    <li class="tf-loop-diagram__step">
      <span class="tf-loop-diagram__num">1</span>
      <div>
        <strong>You set a task</strong>
        <p>Point tsforge at a repo and describe what to change.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tf-loop-diagram__step">
      <span class="tf-loop-diagram__num">2</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Model edits files</strong>
        <p>Tools for read, edit, create, and run. LSP navigation when the repo supports it.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tf-loop-diagram__step">
      <span class="tf-loop-diagram__num">3</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Gate runs for real</strong>
        <p><code>tsc --noEmit</code>, tsforge ESLint, tests when configured.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tf-loop-diagram__step tf-loop-diagram__step--pass">
      <span class="tf-loop-diagram__num">✓</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Pass or repair</strong>
        <p>Exit 0 saves a checkpoint. Failures go back to the model with exact errors.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>
